go channels
go coroutines
connection object to indetify each client (Each net.Conn is a unique object. You could just use the connection itself as the key — map[net.Conn]bool or map[net.Conn]string (where the value is their nickname).)

1. Start the server:
- net.Listen("tcp", ":8080") — opens the port
- listener.Accept() — blocks, returns a net.Conn when someone connects
2. Read from a client:
- bufio.NewScanner(conn) — wraps the connection for easy line reading
- scanner.Scan() — reads one line (blocks until data arrives)
- scanner.Text() — returns the line as a string
3. Send to a client:
- fmt.Fprintf(conn, "message\n") — writes a string to the connection
4. Close:
- conn.Close() — clean up when done
5. Concurrency:
- ch := make(chan string) — create a channel
- ch <- msg — send into channel
- msg := <-ch — receive from channel (blocks)
- go func() { ... }() — launch a goroutine
6. Thread safety:
- var mu sync.Mutex — declare a mutex
- mu.Lock() / mu.Unlock() — protect shared data
7. Cleanup on interrupt:
- os signal.Notify(ch, os.Interrupt) — catch Ctrl+C